    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Located in the peaceful countryside of Oldtown and surrounded by beautiful farmland, this exceptional four-bedroom dormer residence is a wonderfully designed and beautifully presented family home. Set amid large, mature and exceptionally private gardens, the property has been lovingly planned with family life at its core, combining generous living accommodation, an abundance of natural light and excellent outdoor space.\n\nFrom the moment you enter, there is a sense of warmth and character throughout. The accommodation has been thoughtfully arranged to create spaces that work equally well for everyday family living and entertaining. The main reception room is a comfortable and inviting space, with an adjoining playroom providing an ideal dedicated area for younger members of the family while still keeping them close to the main living areas. A separate snug offers another cosy retreat, and two wood-burning fires add further warmth and atmosphere to the home.\n\nAt the heart of the property is the spacious kitchen and dining area, designed as a natural gathering place for family and friends. The kitchen is complemented by a large pantry, providing excellent additional storage, while French doors create a seamless connection between the interior and gardens. A decking area immediately outside the kitchen is perfect for outdoor dining and relaxing, while a separate paved area off the dining space provides another attractive spot from which to enjoy the peaceful surroundings.\n\nThe connection between the house and its gardens is one of the property's particularly appealing features, with French doors from every room opening directly onto the garden. This thoughtful design floods the accommodation with natural light and allows the outdoor spaces to become an extension of the home during the warmer months.\nThe property offers four generously sized bedrooms and four bathrooms, including two en-suites. A particularly useful ground-floor bedroom features sliding wardrobes and a dual-window aspect, creating a bright and airy space, together with a walk-in shower. Its ground-floor position makes it ideal for guests, older children or family members seeking convenient single-level accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, the impressive main bedroom provides a peaceful private retreat and benefits from a walk-in wardrobe. The remaining upstairs bedrooms are equally well considered, with large skylights introducing excellent natural light and adding to the bright, spacious feel of the upper floor.\n\nThe main family bathroom is designed with relaxation in mind, featuring an elegant oval freestanding bath together with a separate shower.\n\nExternally, the property is every bit as impressive. Large, mature gardens surround the house, creating a wonderfully private setting framed by picturesque farmland and open countryside. The grounds have been designed for the whole family to enjoy, including a dedicated children's play area with slide, while the decking and paved terraces provide excellent spaces for outdoor entertaining, summer dining or simply enjoying the tranquillity of the setting.\n\nA separate garage provides valuable additional storage and practical space, while a detached shed of c. 65m2 offers excellent potential for a variety of uses (spp).\n\nBeautifully designed and warmly decorated, this is a home where considerable thought has gone into both the larger living spaces and the smaller practical details. The result is a welcoming and highly versatile family residence that combines comfort, privacy and character with a superb countryside setting.\n\n**Some images may have been digitally enhanced or virtually staged to illustrate the property's potential. All measurements and floor areas are approximate and have been given in good faith. Prospective purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of all details and measurements through their own inspection. **\n\nHighlights:\nOn c. 0.19 hectare/ 0.47-acre site\nInternal area c.214.3m2\nExcellent over all condition\nDetached dormer property\nExtremely spacious accommodation\nDetached shed of c. 65m2 offers excellent potential\nfor a variety of uses (spp)\n4 bedrooms\n3 bathrooms + guest WC\nDetached garage\nLandscaped gardens to the front and rear of the property\nCountryside location\n\n"
      },
